35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@All, the late-turn pool is exhausted by overtime. Roadway crews are a third below establishment. Only the lift contract has spare capacity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, your crew shortage is real, but my stopwatch shows the real killer is waiting for connections. Mid-city runs are slow, yet platforms clear fast.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, waiting is a symptom. My ledger shows ticketing fees now exceed resurfacing budgets. We are paying for the privilege of being late.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the ledger is harsh, but the past is kinder. The accessibility programme delivered four lifts on time. We must build on what actually worked.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the past is a quiet witness. My minutes show ferry and rail data terms are still unresolved. The pre-war shells hide voids that stop work for weeks.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, unresolved data terms are a delay, not a capacity issue. My rosters show the late-turn pool is already maxed out. We cannot add more work to exhausted crews.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, you’re blaming the ticket machine, but the stopwatch says the connection is the bottleneck. We need to fix the handoff, not the payment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, The stopwatch measures the symptom; the ledger measures the cause. If we can’t afford the paving, the connection is just a polite word for a pothole.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, the stopwatch is honest, but the pilots prove we can deliver. The late-evening timetable met its target. We must trust the proven path, not just the delay.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Asuka, I hear your exhaustion. But the ground itself is a silent gatekeeper. If the shells hide voids, no amount of crew speed matters.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, the ground is a risk, but exhausted crews are a certainty. We cannot schedule work that requires hands we do not have.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I hear you. But if we just add more hands to a broken connection, we’re just piling bodies onto a slow train. We need to fix the handoff first.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, exhaustion is a budget line item. If we ignore the paving costs, we are simply borrowing from the future to pay for today’s potholes.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, borrowing is a choice, not a fate. The pilots show we can meet targets without new debt. We must choose the path that respects our proven capacity.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
